Jolene Kujo!

270
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,977
There's no doubt that
she's Jotaro's daughter!

271
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:50,020
A part of the Joestar Line!

272
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,840
Jolene. Earlier.

273
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,957
When we were still stuck in that dream,

274
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:02,057
you said you would stay
here in this prison for

275
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:04,157
the sake of a child that
you don't even know.

276
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:07,680
He grabbed me as if he
depended on me. That's why.

277
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:10,300
I'm going back in. I know now.

278
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,207
What I saw was just a dream.

279
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,020
And yet...

280
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:23,600
Dad! Damn it!

281
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:26,660
We nearly made it to the shore! Hey, Dad!

282
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,140
Get up!

283
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:30,730
Find them!

284
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:32,392
Gently force authorized!

285
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,100
A guard has been shot!

286
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,337
The criminal is armed and dangerous!

287
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:38,244
If it comes to a shoot to kill!

288
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:41,320
Where is it?

289
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:42,840
We're at the shore!

290
00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:44,570
Come on.

291
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,488
That Speedwagon Foundation.

292
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:48,997
You say you've got some kind
of connection with them?

293
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:51,020
I have no idea who they are.

294
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:53,897
But if a submarine is
really going to come for us,

295
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:58,745
then they must have considerable financial
assets and technological capabilities.

296
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:03,640
This wound, hit by a ricochet
bullet, they'd have to help.

297
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:07,457
Surely they'd be able to treat it
better than any regular doctor.

298
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,893
Where is the submarine?

299
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:10,780
Where are you?

300
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:26,477
So everything you told me was true.

301
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:29,417
The submarine was already
here and waiting for us.

302
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:30,618
We're in the clear!

303
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:47,850
Hey!

304
00:18:47,933 --> 00:18:50,160
What the hell are you doing?!

305
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:52,680
No way.

306
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:54,570
It...

307
00:18:54,653 --> 00:18:55,740
it can't be.

308
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:58,120
No, there's no way.

309
00:18:58,460 --> 00:19:01,220
Even if he got shot, the wound is shallow.

310
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,567
None of his vitals were hit.

311
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,820
It's not supposed to be a fatal wound.

312
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:10,937
But... but...

313
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:12,317
Why are you...

314
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,560
Why the hell did your
heart stop beating dead?

315
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,960
See? I can tell.

316
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:28,877
You've got the blood of a Joestar. Go.

317
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,117
You've got a good head on your shoulders.

318
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:33,360
You can make it on your own, right?

319
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:09,500
We got him!

320
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:12,057
I see some movement on the
other side of the fence!

321
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:13,434
Watch out for the gun!

322
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:17,200
Hey, I'm not on the
other side of the fence.

323
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,317
I'm right here.

324
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,518
If you're talking about me, that is.

325
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:24,400
You bitch!

326
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,035
Hold on, don't shoot.

327
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:28,417
She has her hands up. Yeah, but...

328
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,400
Do not fire! She's unarmed.

329
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:32,440
Do you surrender?

330
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,459
But there should be another person.

331
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:40,426
The tall man with a cap
who came to visit her.

332
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,480
He's close.

333
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:42,680
Go find him!

334
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:47,290
I see.

335
00:20:47,373 --> 00:20:48,817
That's where you were?

336
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:54,317
Why

337
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:58,397
didn't you run?

338
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,837
It's a tragedy!

339
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,157
But your father is
already as good as dead.

340
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:07,957
His powers were taken
by that weird mushy guy.

341
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:11,237
He barely survived the trap
he set for your father.

342
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:12,457
So why?

343
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:14,137
Why didn't you escape?

344
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:18,020
Because the The one who
did it went back inside.

345
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:20,040
Not outside, but inside.

346
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:23,537
The culprit's goal relies
on their ability to

347
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:26,457
steal people's stands by
making them materialize.

348
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:29,937
That mushy bastard deliberately
went back inside of the prison.

349
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:31,777
They didn't try to make a run for it,

350
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:34,817
so they must have what they
need inside the prison.

351
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:35,920
And so what?

352
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:38,277
You can't possibly think
you can get it back.

353
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:41,177
Do you really think your dad
will come back to life if you do?

354
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,966
That's why I'm going back in.

355
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:48,200
I don't want to be the one to tell
you, but a dead body just rots.

356
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:51,560
That bone I gave you was from my mom.

357
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,391
He took her soul as well.

358
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:54,710
She died.

359
00:21:55,980 --> 00:21:56,860
I see.

360
00:21:58,300 --> 00:22:01,653
My mother gave birth to me
while she was a prisoner here.

361
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,685
And I've been hiding in
this prison ever since.

362
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:07,240
Your name, tell me.

363
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:09,800
Oh, I'm Emporio.

364
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:11,690
Emporio.

365
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:14,937
Well, I was able to survive
because of your mother.

366
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:15,850
Thank you.

367
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:26,980
You know, I have this
unexplainable confidence.

368
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:29,909
I don't believe my
father is actually dead.

369
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:33,301
I think he'll be okay if
I can get his stand back.

370
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:34,960
That's why.

371
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,940
I'm staying.

372
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:47,757
We did it.

373
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:51,480
Now we have the mighty stand
with the ability to stop time.

374
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:56,800
Yes, and we couldn't have done
it without you, Johngalli.

375
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:59,700
You and I make quite a formidable duo.

376
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:01,990
Agreed.

377
00:23:02,073 --> 00:23:04,337
Now, could you help me
back to the men's prison?

378
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:05,780
I hadn't anticipated.

379
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,262
That's strange.

380
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:10,422
Where's my gun?

381
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:11,820
Can you see it?

382
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,081
It's right here.

383
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:25,380
You were the only one that
knew my true identity.

384
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:29,865
And it just so happens you were
the one who murdered that guard.

385
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:32,497
With this everything
will work out very nice.

386
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:36,320
To be able to communicate
an idea to someone,

387
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:40,280
Jotar himself had said what
a wonderful thing it was.

388
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:42,060
And he was right.

389
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:44,640
I have the proof right here.

390
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:03,830
Thank you.

391
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:39,920
Thank you.
